# `r_oll! n` (B7) gives a random Int from 1 to n, item by item: each
# item of n is a separate roll. Results are random, so these lines
# check what always holds: the range, the shape, the only value of
# `r_oll! 1`, and that many rolls from a large range are not all equal.
== SOURCE
v := r_oll! 1000 r_eshape 6
'& r_/ (v >= 1) & v <= 6
t_ally u_nique v
s_hape r_oll! 2 3 r_eshape 10
r_oll! 1 1 1
'& r_/ (r_oll! 5 10 1000) <= 5 10 1000
1 < t_ally u_nique r_oll! 20 r_eshape 1000000000
== TYPE
v : Int
Bool
Int
Int
Int
Bool
Bool
== RESULT
1
6
2 3
1 1 1
1
1
